{
  "_comment": "Template for a manual supplement, merged in alongside the event-attendance export (member-locations.json) in this same folder. Use this for members who should show on the map even though they don't register for events — e.g. life members. Copy this file to life-members.json (dropping the .example extension) and fill in real entries before running the script — files ending in .json.example are ignored, so a stray placeholder can't leak into the real data. Each entry needs at minimum a name (\"City, ST\" or \"City, Province\") and country; lat/lng are optional and will be geocoded automatically if left null.",
